     The header <_t_g_m_a_t_h_._h> first appeared in FreeBSD 5.3.

CCOOMMPPIILLEERR SSUUPPPPOORRTT
     Before ISO/IEC 9899:2011 (“ISO C11”), the header <_t_g_m_a_t_h_._h> could not be
     implemented with strictly conforming C code and needed special compiler
     support.  As of ISO/IEC 9899:2011 (“ISO C11”), this header file can be
     implemented using the __GGeenneerriicc() language keyword.  In addition to com‐
     pilers that support this keyword, this header file works with GCC.

